WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.264 --> 00:00:08.929
A long time ago, many beavers lived in Scotland.

2
00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:15.493
But their fur became very popular for making coats, and people thought beavers tasted delicious.

3
00:00:16.594 --> 00:00:18.875
They hunted all the beavers until they were gone.

4
00:00:19.856 --> 00:00:21.817
That happened over four hundred years ago.

5
00:00:23.378 --> 00:00:26.980
Today scientists are worried that the beavers have not returned.

6
00:00:28.232 --> 00:00:31.095
So they have decided to learn more about the beaver's habitat.

7
00:00:31.755 --> 00:00:34.578
Habitat means the natural place where an animal lives.

8
00:00:35.118 --> 00:00:40.483
If scientists know more about how beavers live, they can encourage beavers to return to Scotland.

9
00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:46.628
When a beaver turns three years old, it leaves its family and swims downriver to build a new

10
00:00:46.668 --> 00:00:50.071
home. A beaver's home is called a lodge.

11
00:00:51.372 --> 00:00:55.856
It looks like a big pile of sticks, but it is actually a carefully designed house.

12
00:00:57.056 --> 00:01:01.639
Beaver lodges are made of small tree branches and mud that are piled in the shape of an

13
00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:02.939
upside down bowl.

14
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.163
Most lodges are two to three meters high, three to six meters wide, and full of tunnels.

15
00:01:10.744 --> 00:01:13.765
Some tunnels lead to the rooms inside where the beavers live.

16
00:01:14.586 --> 00:01:15.767
Other tunnels store food.

17
00:01:16.487 --> 00:01:22.210
There are also secret tunnels that confuse predators—so hungry animals don't make beaver soup for dinner!

18
00:01:23.211 --> 00:01:28.918
Beavers build their lodges in streams, and the entrance is always underwater so that it is hard to

19
00:01:28.978 --> 00:01:33.962
find. For a long time, scientists were confused about the size of a beaver lodge.

20
00:01:34.822 --> 00:01:40.266
Most beaver families have a mom, a dad, and one to four babies, which are called kits.

21
00:01:41.187 --> 00:01:42.788
Why did they need so much room?

22
00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:48.772
After watching beavers for a long time, scientists found two answers to their question.

23
00:01:50.192 --> 00:01:55.156
First, beavers build big homes because they need thick walls to keep out predators.

24
00:01:56.596 --> 00:01:59.377
Second, beavers need a place to store their food.

25
00:02:00.278 --> 00:02:05.560
Since beavers do not hibernate, they need a warm, safe place and lots of food when the weather

26
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.200
gets cold.

27
00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.442
In the north many lakes turn to ice in the winter.

28
00:02:12.522 --> 00:02:18.425
The ice often traps beavers inside their lodge, so beavers need to store enough food to make sure

29
00:02:18.465 --> 00:02:19.545
they don't get hungry.

30
00:02:21.766 --> 00:02:27.893
Beavers will often build their lodge with young trees on the inside so they can eat the bark

31
00:02:27.953 --> 00:02:28.574
during winter.

32
00:02:30.235 --> 00:02:34.338
Beavers love to eat bark, especially from aspen and cottonwood trees.

33
00:02:35.219 --> 00:02:40.703
Beavers also like to eat clover and raspberry bushes, but their favorite food is water lilies.

34
00:02:41.524 --> 00:02:44.867
Many people think beavers eat fish, but this is not true.

35
00:02:46.308 --> 00:02:50.191
The best way to find a beaver habitat is to look for a lot of water.

36
00:02:50.911 --> 00:02:53.293
Beavers always build a dam near their lodge.

37
00:02:54.034 --> 00:02:56.536
It makes the stream slow down and creates a pond.

38
00:02:57.216 --> 00:03:01.437
This way the lodge is surrounded by water, making it look like a tiny island.

39
00:03:04.078 --> 00:03:09.800
After watching beavers for a long time, scientists learned that beavers live for about ten years.

40
00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.201
Once two beavers decide to make a family, they never leave each other.

41
00:03:15.381 --> 00:03:19.383
Beavers somehow always know when there are too many beavers living on their river.

42
00:03:20.843 --> 00:03:24.124
They have the right-sized family to keep the river from getting crowded.

43
00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.327
Now that the scientists know what beavers like to eat, where they like to live, and how they

44
00:03:30.347 --> 00:03:35.013
build their homes, they are working to make Scotland a place that beavers can call home.
